# Agent Ownership

Use [`../../docs/agent-architecture.md`](../../docs/agent-architecture.md) as the shared routing policy. Specialist prompts in `.cursor/agents/` describe optional skills, not mandatory steps.

- Assign one implementing owner per file for each work stage.
- A reviewer or validator does not silently edit the files being reviewed.
- For a small isolated patch, implementation plus a targeted check is enough.
- Add independent review when a contract, cross-contour boundary, data integrity, private send path, or production conclusion makes the change high risk.
- D↔B work must state which side owns each change and how the other side is protected.
- Keep the required live-send gates and separate explicit permission for a live action. A testnet/demo run is the preferred staged check where supported; skipping it requires explicit risk acceptance.
- Do not create permanent roles for a single task or start several agents on the same files.
